<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ADR-015 / PRD §5.3.

  ★ <uses-policies> is deliberately EMPTY. ★

  None of the powers Kavach actually needs — user restrictions, permission grant
  policy, uninstall blocking, Factory Reset Protection — come from this file.
  They come from being Device Owner. What this file *would* grant, if we listed
  the usual boilerplate, is <wipe-data> and <reset-password>: the ability to
  erase a family's phone and to change the lock screen credential.

  A safety app that can wipe the device it is protecting is a hostage situation,
  not a safety app (P-006). If a future feature genuinely needs one of these
  policies, add exactly that one, and nothing else, in the same commit as the
  guardian-facing consent screen that explains it.
-->
<device-admin xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:visible="false">
    <uses-policies />
</device-admin>
